### How does setInputFiles work for standard file inputs?

For a standard HTML file input, locate the input and call setInputFiles with the file path. Playwright sets the file directly without opening the OS dialog.

```typescript
// Single file upload
await page.getByLabel('Upload Document').setInputFiles('fixtures/address-proof.pdf');

// Multiple files (input must have 'multiple' attribute)
await page.getByLabel('Upload Documents').setInputFiles([
  'fixtures/id-proof.pdf',
  'fixtures/address-proof.pdf',
]);

// Clear a selection
await page.getByLabel('Upload Document').setInputFiles([]);
```

### How do you upload from memory without a fixture file?

Pass an object with name, MIME type, and buffer to generate test files on the fly.

```typescript
// In-memory file: no fixture needed
await page.getByLabel('Upload Statement').setInputFiles({
  name: 'statement-2024.csv',
  mimeType: 'text/csv',
  buffer: Buffer.from(
    'Date,Description,Amount\n2024-01-15,Salary Credit,50000.00\n'
  ),
});

// Generate a synthetic PDF
import { randomBytes } from 'crypto';
await page.getByLabel('Upload Document').setInputFiles({
  name: 'test-doc.pdf',
  mimeType: 'application/pdf',
  buffer: Buffer.from('%PDF-1.4 ' + randomBytes(100).toString('hex')),
});
```

### How do you handle custom upload controls with filechooser?

For custom controls that open the native file dialog on click, capture the filechooser event.

```typescript
// Custom upload: intercept the file chooser dialog
const fileChooserPromise = page.waitForEvent('filechooser');
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Choose File' }).click();
const fileChooser = await fileChooserPromise;

// Set the file on the chooser
await fileChooser.setFiles('fixtures/address-proof.pdf');

// Check if multiple files are accepted
console.log('Accepts multiple:', fileChooser.isMultiple());
```

### How do you verify the upload client-side?

Assert the UI reflects the successful upload using auto-waiting assertions.

```typescript
// Client-side verification
await page.getByLabel('Upload Document').setInputFiles('fixtures/id-proof.pdf');

// File name appears
await expect(page.getByText('id-proof.pdf')).toBeVisible();

// Upload progress completes
await expect(page.getByTestId('upload-progress')).toHaveAttribute(
  'aria-valuenow', '100'
);

// Success message
await expect(page.getByText('Document uploaded successfully')).toBeVisible();
```

### How do you verify the upload server-side?

Server-side verification is stronger. Assert the document exists via API with correct metadata.

```typescript
// Server-side verification via API
const response = await page.request.get(
  '/api/accounts/ACC-001/documents'
);
const documents = await response.json();

const uploaded = documents.find(
  (d: any) => d.name === 'id-proof.pdf'
);
expect(uploaded).toBeDefined();
expect(uploaded.type).toBe('application/pdf');
expect(uploaded.size).toBeGreaterThan(0);
```

### How do you test negative upload cases?

Disallowed types and oversized files must be rejected with the correct error.

```typescript
// Negative: disallowed file type
await page.getByLabel('Upload Document').setInputFiles({
  name: 'malware.exe',
  mimeType: 'application/octet-stream',
  buffer: Buffer.from('fake executable'),
});
await expect(
  page.getByText('File type not allowed')
).toBeVisible();

// Negative: oversized file (simulate with large buffer)
await page.getByLabel('Upload Document').setInputFiles({
  name: 'huge-file.pdf',
  mimeType: 'application/pdf',
  buffer: Buffer.alloc(11 * 1024 * 1024), // 11MB
});
await expect(
  page.getByText('File exceeds maximum size')
).toBeVisible();
```

### What is the complete upload test pattern?

A complete upload test covers the happy path, server verification, and negative cases.

```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.describe('Document Upload', () => {
  test('Upload address proof and verify', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/onboarding/documents');
    await page.getByLabel('Address Proof').setInputFiles(
      'fixtures/address-proof.pdf'
    );
    await expect(page.getByText('address-proof.pdf')).toBeVisible();
    await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }).click();
    await expect(page.getByText('Document uploaded')).toBeVisible();

    // Verify server-side
    const docs = await (await page.request.get(
      '/api/accounts/ACC-001/documents'
    )).json();
    expect(docs.some((d: any) => d.name === 'address-proof.pdf')).toBe(true);
  });

  test('Reject executable file', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/onboarding/documents');
    await page.getByLabel('Address Proof').setInputFiles({
      name: 'script.exe',
      mimeType: 'application/octet-stream',
      buffer: Buffer.from('fake'),
    });
    await expect(page.getByText('File type not allowed')).toBeVisible();
  });
});
```

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- "When should you use setInputFiles vs filechooser?" Prefer setInputFiles when a real file input exists. Use filechooser only for custom controls that open the OS dialog.
- "How do you test drag-and-drop uploads?" Playwright's dragTo or dispatchEvent can simulate drag-and-drop, but setInputFiles on the underlying input is often simpler and more reliable.
- "Should you commit binary test fixtures?" Prefer in-memory buffers for small files. Only commit binary fixtures when the file content matters for the test.
